            </span>
            <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-stone-900 sm:text-3xl">Gypsum</h2>
          </div>
          <div class="mt-6 grid items-center gap-8 sm:grid-cols-5">
            <p class="leading-7 text-stone-600 sm:col-span-3">
              Gypsum is a naturally occurring mineral, widely used in the
              construction and agricultural industries. Our gypsum products
              are known for their high purity and consistency, making them
              ideal for a range of applications.
            </p>
            <img
              src="data:image/jpeg;base64,"
              alt="Gypsum crystal specimen"
              class="aspect-[4/3] w-full rounded-2xl object-cover shadow-sm sm:col-span-2"
              loading="lazy"
            />
          </div>
          <dl class="mt-8 grid gap-8 sm:grid-cols-3">
            <div>
              <dt class="text-base font-semibold text-amber-800">Construction</dt>
              <dd class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-stone-600">
                Gypsum is a key ingredient in the production of plaster,
                drywall, and cement. Its properties help improve the fire
                resistance, soundproofing, and finish of buildings.
              </dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt class="text-base font-semibold text-amber-800">Agriculture</dt>
              <dd class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-stone-600">
                Gypsum is used as a soil conditioner, improving soil
                structure and fertility. It helps in reducing soil erosion
                and provides essential calcium and sulfur to crops.
              </dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt class="text-base font-semibold text-amber-800">Industrial Processes</dt>
              <dd class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-stone-600">
                Gypsum is also utilized in the manufacturing of cement, as
                a filler in paper and textiles, and in the production of
                glass and ceramics.
              </dd>
            </div>
          </dl>
          <p class="mt-8 max-w-3xl border-l-2 border-amber-700 pl-4 text-sm italic leading-6 text-stone-500">
            We offer both natural gypsum and salt pan gypsum, each suited
            for different industrial and agricultural needs.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="limestone" class="reveal scroll-mt-32 py-16">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-4">
            <span class="flex h-12 w-12 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-xl bg-amber-100 text-amber-800">
              <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" class="h-6 w-6"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M3 20l4-9 4 5 3-7 4 6 3-3v8H3z" /></svg>
            </span>
            <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-stone-900 sm:text-3xl">Limestone</h2>
          </div>
          <div class="mt-6 grid items-center gap-8 sm:grid-cols-5">
            <img
              src="data:image/jpeg;base64,"
              alt="Limestone rock specimen"
              class="aspect-[4/3] w-full rounded-2xl object-cover shadow-sm sm:col-span-2"
              loading="lazy"
            />
            <p class="leading-7 text-stone-600 sm:col-span-3">
              Limestone is a sedimentary rock, primarily composed of calcium
              carbonate, and is one of the most versatile minerals in the
              world. Our limestone products are of the highest purity,
              ensuring they meet the stringent requirements of various
              industries.
            </p>
          </div>
          <dl class="mt-8 grid gap-8 sm:grid-cols-3">
            <div>
              <dt class="text-base font-semibold text-amber-800">Cement Production</dt>
              <dd class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-stone-600">
                Limestone is a critical raw material in the production of
                cement. It is calcined to produce lime, which is then
                combined with other materials to form clinker, the
                precursor to cement.
              </dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt class="text-base font-semibold text-amber-800">Construction</dt>
              <dd class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-stone-600">
                Beyond cement, limestone is used as an aggregate in
                construction projects, providing a strong base for roads,
                buildings, and other infrastructure.
              </dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt class="text-base font-semibold text-amber-800">Environmental Applications</dt>
              <dd class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-stone-600">
                Limestone is used in environmental applications, such as
                flue gas desulfurization, where it helps reduce sulfur
                emissions from industrial processes.
              </dd>
            </div>
          </dl>
          <p class="mt-8 max-w-3xl border-l-2 border-amber-700 pl-4 text-sm italic leading-6 text-stone-500">
            Our limestone products are available in different grades to
            suit specific industrial needs.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="manganese-ore" class="reveal scroll-mt-32 py-16">
