          <dl class="mt-8 grid gap-8 sm:grid-cols-3">
            <div>
              <dt class="text-base font-semibold text-amber-800">Ceramics</dt>
              <dd class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-stone-600">
                China clay is a key ingredient in the production of
                porcelain and fine china, where it provides the necessary
                plasticity and strength to the ceramic body. It is also
                used in the production of sanitaryware and tiles.
              </dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt class="text-base font-semibold text-amber-800">Paper Industry</dt>
              <dd class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-stone-600">
                In the paper industry, china clay is used as a filler and
                coating material, improving the brightness, smoothness,
                and printability of paper products.
              </dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt class="text-base font-semibold text-amber-800">Paints and Coatings</dt>
              <dd class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-stone-600">
                China clay is used as a pigment and extender in paints and
                coatings, where it enhances the opacity, texture, and
                durability of the final product.
              </dd>
            </div>
          </dl>
          <p class="mt-8 max-w-3xl border-l-2 border-amber-700 pl-4 text-sm italic leading-6 text-stone-500">
            Our china clay is available in various grades to meet the
            specific requirements of different industries.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="fly-ash" class="reveal scroll-mt-32 py-16">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-4">
            <span class="flex h-12 w-12 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-xl bg-amber-100 text-amber-800">
              <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" class="h-6 w-6"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M6 18a4 4 0 010-8 5 5 0 019.6-1.5A4.5 4.5 0 0119 18H6z" /></svg>
            </span>
            <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-stone-900 sm:text-3xl">Fly Ash</h2>
          </div>
          <div class="mt-6 grid items-center gap-8 sm:grid-cols-5">
            <img
              src="data:image/jpeg;base64,"
              alt="Thermal power plant, source of fly ash"
              class="aspect-[4/3] w-full rounded-2xl object-cover shadow-sm sm:col-span-2"
              loading="lazy"
            />
            <p class="leading-7 text-stone-600 sm:col-span-3">
              Fly ash is a fine powder, a byproduct of coal combustion in
              power plants. Our fly ash products are of high quality,
              making them suitable for use in construction and other
              industrial applications.
            </p>
          </div>
          <dl class="mt-8 grid gap-8 sm:grid-cols-3">
            <div>
              <dt class="text-base font-semibold text-amber-800">Concrete Production</dt>
              <dd class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-stone-600">
                Fly ash is commonly used as a partial replacement for
                cement in concrete production. It improves the
                workability, strength, and durability of concrete, while
                also reducing the overall cost and environmental impact.
              </dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt class="text-base font-semibold text-amber-800">Road Construction</dt>
              <dd class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-stone-600">
                In road construction, fly ash is used as a stabilizer for
                soils and as a component in asphalt mixtures, improving
                the strength and longevity of roads.
              </dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt class="text-base font-semibold text-amber-800">Environmental Applications</dt>
              <dd class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-stone-600">
                Fly ash is also used in environmental applications, such
                as waste stabilization and mine reclamation, where it
                helps improve soil structure and reduce environmental
                hazards.
              </dd>
            </div>
          </dl>
          <p class="mt-8 max-w-3xl border-l-2 border-amber-700 pl-4 text-sm italic leading-6 text-stone-500">
            Our fly ash products are available in different grades to
            meet the specific needs of construction and environmental
            projects.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="cement-clinker" class="reveal scroll-mt-32 py-16">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-4">
            <span class="flex h-12 w-12 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-xl bg-amber-100 text-amber-800">
              <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" class="h-6 w-6"><rect x="4" y="4" width="7" height="7" rx="1" /><rect x="13" y="4" width="7" height="7" rx="1" /><rect x="4" y="13" width="7" height="7" rx="1" /><rect x="13" y="13" width="7" height="7" rx="1" /></svg>
            </span>
            <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-stone-900 sm:text-3xl">Cement Clinker</h2>
          </div>
          <div class="mt-6 grid items-center gap-8 sm:grid-cols-5">
            <p class="leading-7 text-stone-600 sm:col-span-3">
              Cement clinker is a crucial component in the production of
              cement. It is formed by heating limestone and other materials
              in a kiln, creating a hard, nodular material that is then
              ground to produce cement. Our cement clinker is sourced from
              top manufacturers, ensuring consistent quality and
              performance.
            </p>
            <img
              src="data:image/jpeg;base64,"
              alt="Cement clinker nodules"
              class="aspect-[4/3] w-full rounded-2xl object-cover shadow-sm sm:col-span-2"
              loading="lazy"
            />
          </div>
          <dl class="mt-8 grid gap-8 sm:grid-cols-3">
            <div>
              <dt class="text-base font-semibold text-amber-800">Cement Production</dt>
              <dd class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-stone-600">
                Cement clinker is ground with gypsum and other additives
                to produce various types of cement. It provides the
                necessary properties for cement to set and harden, making
                it a key ingredient in construction.
              </dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt class="text-base font-semibold text-amber-800">Construction</dt>
              <dd class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-stone-600">
                Cement clinker is used in the construction of buildings,
                bridges, roads, and other infrastructure projects, where
                it provides the strength and durability needed for
                long-lasting structures.
              </dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt class="text-base font-semibold text-amber-800">Specialty Applications</dt>
              <dd class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-stone-600">
                Cement clinker can be tailored to produce different types
                of cement, such as Portland cement, white cement, and
                oil-well cement, each suited for specific construction
                needs.
              </dd>
            </div>
          </dl>
          <p class="mt-8 max-w-3xl border-l-2 border-amber-700 pl-4 text-sm italic leading-6 text-stone-500">
            Our cement clinker is available in different grades to meet
            the specific requirements of cement manufacturers and
            construction projects.
          </p>
        </section>
      </div>
